        "summary": "This article shares the inspiring story of Bill Allison, an 81-year-old military veteran who received a heart transplant in 2009 after decades of smoking and two heart attacks. It highlights his life-changing decision to quit smoking and drinking, emphasizing the critical role of ongoing medical care and medication adherence, supported by CVS Specialty and his pharmacist, Amy Guard. The piece also underscores the profound impact of organ donation and encourages others to consider becoming donors and to listen to their healthcare teams.",
