        "source": "Richmondside",
        "source_domain": "Richmondside",
        "summary": "The Asian Pacific Environmental Network (APEN), founded in Richmond three decades ago, has grown into a formidable three-office organization with 40 staff and nearly 1,000 members. APEN has achieved significant victories against Chevron, including a $550 million settlement for Richmond in 2024, and has been instrumental in advocating for environmental justice for historically marginalized communities like Laotian refugees. With new co-director Michelle Chan, APEN is now focusing on helping Richmond transition to a cleaner economy by collaborating with city leaders to wisely spend settlement funds and develop contingency plans for the eventual closure of fossil fuel refineries.",
